  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "L1",
      "chunk_id": "L1",
      "delivery": "intense",
      "text": "Police force their way into your home with a warrant that doesn't exist — and search everything you own.",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.526,
      "seconds": 5.526,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:94faba0376a02bfd9a1f4682c20828b9ef475dbfa322c1fa9c2b6c680eabc790"
    },
    {
      "id": "L2",
      "chunk_id": "L2",
      "delivery": "building",
      "text": "For most of American history, evidence taken in an illegal search could still be used to convict you. The search being illegal simply didn't matter.",
      "start": 6.246,
      "end": 13.769,
      "seconds": 7.523,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:f3f2403e09cbd77f48849da2c2690a5b7d1f4d42e5a48d93d453d6efdc3d64d2"
    },
    {
      "id": "L3",
      "chunk_id": "L3",
      "delivery": "building",
      "text": "Then officers pushed into Dollree Mapp's home, waving a piece of paper they claimed was a warrant, and searched her entire house.",
      "start": 14.489,
      "end": 21.083,
      "seconds": 6.594,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:e051e4aaef058b97c42964b9055274dd2159a69ef4a7cff13c0cffed643457f2"
    },
    {
      "id": "L4",
      "chunk_id": "L4",
      "delivery": "intense",
      "text": "In nineteen sixty-one, the Supreme Court drew the line. Evidence from an illegal search can't be used against you — in any state. A search that breaks the rules now protects you.",
      "start": 21.803,
      "end": 31.88,
      "seconds": 10.077,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:cf4a552bf9f8ace7ba9dcc8f90ccb0eb8f7cf9690c8e4372c43e1585d5f8fbba"
    },
    {
      "id": "L5",
      "chunk_id": "L5",
      "delivery": "calm",
      "text": "Watch the full story on the channel. Follow for more.",
      "start": 32.6,
      "end": 35.294,
      "seconds": 2.694,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:278f3673f5a6d7fb0157ed20c23bfbed67490a212977fab0a27aaaaee99a2cd5"
    }
  ]
}
